Side $AC$ of $\triangle ABC$ is extended to $D$. Name the two interior angles opposite $\angle BCD$, then write an exterior-angle equation.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);\coordinate (B) at (1.4,2.4);\coordinate (C) at (4,0);\coordinate (D) at (5.6,0);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;\draw (C)--(D);
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};\node[above] at (B) {$B$};\node[below] at (C) {$C$};\node[below] at (D) {$D$};
\node at (0.65,0.35) {$p$};\node at (1.55,1.75) {$q$};\node at (4.4,0.4) {$r$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

